  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}({t}^{2}+t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}{e}^{t+1} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+1)}{t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}+(-1) \\\\ {e}^{-1+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-1+1)}{(-1)}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+1) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}2 \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}\\frac{1-2t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-1+1) \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{1-2(-1)}{(-1)^{2}+1})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}[3f(t)-2g(t)] & =3{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}f(t)-2{lim}_{t\\to \\,-1}g(t) \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
